    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hu">Hu</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="194" ed="#liebermann"/>On hundrede swa on oðer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.1"/> gemote we wyllað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mon folcriht getæce æt ælcere spǽce, ⁊ andagie, hwænne man þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> gelæste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="194" ed="#liebermann"/>In hundredo sicut in alio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.1-2"/> (omni) placito uolumus, ut rectum (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.5-2"/> ius) pupplicum iudicetur in omni causa, et adterminetur, quando hoc impleatur.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="195" ed="#liebermann"/>In centenariis necnon et in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.4"/> aliis placitis uolumus, ut puplica rectitudo (teneatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.2"/> uel) decernatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.5"/> in omni causa (inter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.3"/> uirum et uirum), et ut inducietur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.6"/>, donec perficiatur (rectitudo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_7.lnote.oe.3"/>).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="7" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="18" ed="#robertson"/>On hundrede swa on oðer gemote we wyllað þæt mon folcriht getæce æt ælcere spǽce, ⁊ andagie hwænne man þæt gelæste.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="195" ed="#liebermann"/>Im Hundred wie im anderen Gericht wollen wir, dass bei jeder Klage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Hu_7.lnote.de.1"/> Volksrecht angeordnet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_7.lnote.de.2"/> und Termin gestellt werde, wann man das [Urtheil] erfüllen werde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">In the hundred as in any other court we will that folk-right be ordered in every suit, and a term be set for when the [judgment] is to be fulfilled.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="19" ed="#robertson"/>In the hundred, as in other courts<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Hu_7.robnote.n.1"/>, it is our will that every case be treated in accordance with the public law and have a date fixed for its decision.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="433" ed="#whitelock"/>In the hundred, as in any other court, it is our will that in every suit the common law be enjoined, and a day appointed when it shall be carried out.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="195"><ref target="clause:IEw_Prol">I Ew Pr.</ref>; <ref target="clause:IIEw_8">II Ew 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. I Ew. Pr.; II 8</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="196"><ref target="clause:Ine_8">Ine 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="196"><ref target="clause:IIEw_8">II Ew 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="316"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_1-1">III Eg 1.1–4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="316"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5–5.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="195"><ref target="clause:IICn_15-2">II Cn 15.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Ew Pr.; II [Ew] 8.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Glosse</hi>) <hi rend="italic">aus Hk; fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(gloss) from Hk; lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">disc. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">disc. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Glosse</hi>) <hi rend="italic">aus Hr; fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(gloss) from Hr; lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">indicetur <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">indicetur Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond;</hi> (<hi rend="italic">eingeklammertes</hi>) <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">before the bracket Lond; (bracketed) the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et ius <hi rend="italic">nicht Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et ius not in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gericht 11.—Auch III Eg 1, 1 verbindet dieselben zwei Eadward-Stellen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gericht 11.—III Eg 1, 1 too combines the same two passages of Eadward</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘zuerkannt, geurteilt’; Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 208. Nicht etwa ‘weisen’ im Sinne des Gesetzsprechers</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘adjudged, judged’; Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 208. Not, say, ‘declare’ in the sense of the lawspeaker</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Hu_7.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The nature of the meetings mentioned in the earlier laws is not specified. It cannot be determined for certain whether such meetings as those mentioned, for example, in Af. 38 are of identical character with those mentioned in II Edw. 8. From this time onwards, as Liebermann observes, we hear of meetings (or courts) of the hundred, the borough, and the county, as well as of the court of the Five Boroughs (<hi rend="italic">Fif Burga geþincðu</hi>) in the N.E. Midlands. References are also found to joint meetings of several hundreds, <hi rend="italic">e.g. Liber Eliensis</hi>, ed. Stewart, Bk. <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. Chap. 11 (pp. 129–30), Chap. 34 (p. 151).</seg></note>
      </div>
